# Test Case Standards — Priority, Type & Requirement Mapping

Every automated test case **must** declare **priority**, **suite type**, and at least one **requirement ID** from `requirements_document.md`.

## 1. Test Priority

Derive priority from `risk_analysis.md`. Map risk level to test priority:

| Priority | Risk Level | When to Use | Execution Order |
|----------|------------|-------------|-----------------|
| **P1** | High | Auth, payments, checkout, discounts, invoices, RBAC, admin user/order mgmt | Run first |
| **P2** | Medium | Catalog, rentals, profile, favorites, chat, APIs, admin CRUD | Run second |
| **P3** | Low | i18n, privacy, contact form, comparison, cosmetic/UX | Run last |

- Every **P1** test must have at least one matching `REQ-*` ID.
- Cross-cutting scenarios from `risk_analysis.md` § Cross-Cutting High-Risk Scenarios are always **P1** and **E2E**.

## 2. Test Suite Type

Assign **one primary** suite type per test. Add secondary tags only when the test legitimately belongs to multiple suites.

| Type | Tag | Purpose | Typical Scope | Run Frequency |
|------|-----|---------|---------------|---------------|
| **Smoke** | `@smoke` | Fast critical-path sanity | Happy path only; 1–3 steps per feature area | Every build / PR |
| **Regression** | `@regression` | Feature-depth & validation | Individual ACs, edge cases, negative paths, API contract | Nightly / release |
| **E2E** | `@e2e` | Multi-module user journeys | Full workflows spanning 2+ modules (e.g. browse → cart → checkout → invoice) | Nightly / pre-release |

### Classification Rules

- **Smoke** — Can the app ship if this fails? If yes → not smoke. Examples: login, product grid load, add to cart, guest checkout happy path, `POST /users/login`, `GET /products`.
- **Regression** — Single-feature or single-endpoint validation. Examples: search min/max length, payment field validation, account locking after 3 attempts, gift card 422 response.
- **E2E** — End-to-end journey across modules. Examples: authenticated purchase with PDF download, guest checkout + combination discount, TOTP login during checkout, chat widget checkout.

### API Coverage Tiers (from `requirements_document.md` §2)

| API Tier | Maps To | Tag |
|----------|---------|-----|
| Smoke (8 endpoints) | Critical-path API checks | `@smoke` `@api` |
| Regression (28 public) | Full public contract | `@regression` `@api` |
| Regression Auth (24) | Customer token / 401 / owner-only | `@regression` `@api` |
| Regression Admin (27) | Admin CRUD / 403 for customers | `@regression` `@api` |

Layer tag: add `@ui` or `@api` alongside suite tags.

## 3. Requirement Mapping

### Source of Truth

| Document | Use For |
|----------|---------|
| `requirements_document.md` | Requirement IDs (`REQ-S*`, `REQ-BR-*`, `REQ-RBAC-*`, `REQ-API-*`) |
| `requirements_document.csv` | Bulk lookup, filtering, coverage reports |
| `Application_Context.md` | Behavior context when AC text is ambiguous |

### ID Prefixes

| Prefix | Example | Maps To |
|--------|---------|---------|
| `REQ-S{n}-` | `REQ-S5-PO-001` | Sprint user-story acceptance criterion |
| `REQ-BR-` | `REQ-BR-012` | Business rule (§4) |
| `REQ-RBAC-` | `REQ-RBAC-003` | Role-based access rule (§2) |
| `REQ-API-` | `REQ-API-PRD-001` | REST API endpoint coverage (§6) |

### Mapping Workflow (required before writing a test)

1. Read feature behavior in `Application_Context.md`.
2. Find the matching row(s) in `requirements_document.md` or `.csv` by module and AC title.
3. Confirm priority from `risk_analysis.md` for that feature area.
4. Choose suite type (smoke / regression / E2E) per §2 above.
5. Embed the `REQ-*` ID(s) in the test — never invent IDs.

### Traceability Rules

- **One test → one or more REQ IDs.** Multi-REQ allowed for E2E journeys; list all covered IDs.
- **One REQ → one or more tests** allowed (smoke + regression + negative variants).
- Prefer **Sprint 5** IDs (`REQ-S5-*`) for current-platform UI tests unless testing a specific sprint environment.
- API tests map to `REQ-API-*`; business-rule validations map to `REQ-BR-*`; access-control tests map to `REQ-RBAC-*`.

## 4. Playwright Conventions

### Test Title Format

```
[REQ-S5-PO-001] [P1] [Smoke] Product grid is displayed on home page
```

Order: **Requirement ID** → **Priority** → **Suite Type** → **Human-readable title**

### Tags & Annotations

```typescript
test('[REQ-S5-PO-001] [P1] [Smoke] Product grid is displayed', {
  tag: ['@smoke', '@p1', '@ui'],
  annotation: [
    { type: 'requirement', description: 'REQ-S5-PO-001' },
    { type: 'priority', description: 'P1' },
    { type: 'suite', description: 'smoke' },
  ],
}, async ({ page }) => {
  // ...
});
```

### Describe-Block Grouping

Group tests by module and requirement prefix:

```typescript
test.describe('Product Overview @regression', () => {
  test.describe('REQ-S5-PO', () => {
    // tests for REQ-S5-PO-001 through REQ-S5-PO-013
  });
});
```

### Running by Tag

```bash
npx playwright test --grep @smoke
npx playwright test --grep "@regression|@e2e"
npx playwright test --grep @p1
npx playwright test --grep "REQ-S5-CC-CART"
```

## 5. Coverage Checklist

Before merging new tests, verify:

- [ ] At least one `REQ-*` ID per test (in title or annotation)
- [ ] Priority (`P1`/`P2`/`P3`) matches `risk_analysis.md` for the feature
- [ ] Suite type tag (`@smoke`, `@regression`, or `@e2e`) is set
- [ ] Layer tag (`@ui` or `@api`) is set
- [ ] REQ ID exists in `requirements_document.md` or `.csv`
